WEBVTT

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:46.240
Just a little further, Mr. Fairy.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:48.280
It'll be all right.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:06.100
Mistel T-1...

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:11.070
Proceed to Cleveland Air Force Base
immediately after refueling.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.370
Could it be...

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:17.020
The documentation was fine.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:23.880
I have no idea how that bomb
got replaced, or who did it.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:26.000
And so?

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.300
Evacuate HQ as planned.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.390
And keep this confidential.

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:36.160
That's easier said.

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:47.510
No change in target's speed.

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:50.380
Contact with HQ in 115 minutes.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:53.690
Delete all data below level C.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:56.190
And destroy all media.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:59.580
Non-combat and combat
personnel with B clearance...

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:02.090
...are to work on media disposal.

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:03.060
Repeat.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:06.290
Non-combat and combat
personnel with B clearance...

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:08.660
...are to work on media disposal.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.100
Shall we go soon?

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:16.710
Mr. Fairy's coming with us.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:18.770
There's nowhere for me to go.

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:20.710
That's not true!

00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:25.410
Wherever you go, people will be
nice to you because you're special.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:29.750
I was told that there's no
such place as the land of the fairies.

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:33.660
This is the only place
Mr. Fairy and I have left.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.230
Who told you that?

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.790
No! No! No!

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:43.100
I hate this!

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.730
I don't want to go anywhere else!

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:52.000
Commander!

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:54.250
Will we really just abandon this place?

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.170
You have your orders.

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:58.210
Ready the flight plans.

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:00.240
Wait, Commander...

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:01.810
What do you propose?

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:07.520
We thought we had an ace in the hole...

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:09.770
...but it all turned out to be a bad beat.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:13.240
We don't have any more cards in our hand.

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:18.620
No, we still have one left.

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:21.490
You can't mean that...

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:22.780
I can.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:24.460
Please, let us do it.

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:28.370
On behalf of all of us...

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.330
...give us one last chance.

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:33.380
It's orders from above.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:35.180
We still can't follow them.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:36.680
Why?

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:37.620
Because-

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:41.590
Lt. Simmons and I have already
lost a lot of comrades in this war.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:46.800
I never want to lose a unit
I ought to bring back again.

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:51.450
You mean the 16th Air Force Unit.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:55.840
But Funeral will still exist.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:57.980
All we're losing is our base.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:00.510
That means nothing.

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:01.940
Lt. Green...

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:05.020
...isn't that what you said in the Air Force?

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:07.720
That this is a fight for our existence?

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:09.820
That there's no retreat?

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:14.120
Hattie said she doesn't want to leave
because this is her home.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:21.270
It's a pretty flimsy home to cling to.

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:25.640
No warm fireplace or flower bed
to comfort our minds.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:28.850
No, I know you feel
the same way, Commander.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:34.450
And you, Lt. Soma?

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:36.730
I'd like to hear your opinion.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.230
We need to stand and fight.

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:41.190
I see.

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:45.730
We should use everything
Funeral has, including the EX-1.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:57.130
Confirm the heavy strength alien jammers.

00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:58.340
Huh?

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:01.300
We may lose some important level A data.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.980
Close all contact with the outside.

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:05.180
Commander?

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:08.640
That way no one can tell us to evacuate.

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:14.580
I'll put all of this in my report.

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:16.800
If the base is still here.

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:20.560
All right, let's move.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:22.650
We have to defend our home.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:48.510
Now we're both on the Titanic.

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:52.890
You and me, let's sink together.

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:05.490
All fliers and particle bombers but
damaged ones should be in the sky.

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:19.210
All troops classified B or less
should evacuate immediately.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.890
We have 30 minutes.

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:23.190
Commander.

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:25.360
Didn't you hear what I said?

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:26.800
Let us help out.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:29.770
You might die, you know.

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:33.480
This badge on our chests
isn’t just an accessory.

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:37.550
Acknowledged.

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:44.640
It hasn't been touched since the last test.

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:46.120
But it still might work.

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:49.980
Then this is truly the last card
we have to play.

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:53.450
But no casino would take a bad bet like this.

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:59.050
You made such a big decision.

00:07:59.050 --> 00:08:05.050
A woman's duty to look after her home
is an old tradition, isn't it?

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:07.730
I think it's a right way of thinking.

00:08:07.730 --> 00:08:12.040
Just think of this whole planet,
not just the base, as our home.

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:17.230
Thank you, Captain.

00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:25.870
I'm sorry, Harriet.

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:29.330
You can call to your fairy
from here, can't you?

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:31.080
Sure!

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:34.660
The target is within visual range.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:43.930
Looks like he's received our party invitation.

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:47.670
Welcome to Funeral, Mr. Alien.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:20.340
Formation Alpha!

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:35.440
Target's speed at zero.

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:37.650
Start the Fefnir!

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:45.990
Electromagnetic field adjustment complete.

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:47.610
Barrel charge ready.

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:55.710
Discharging bolt at 22.7 gigawatts.

00:09:56.010 --> 00:10:00.710
Built at the turn of the century
at great expense...

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:04.050
...the world's largest charged
particle accelerator, Fefnir.

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:13.260
After this plan was aborted,
the military took over.

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:18.940
It may truly be the last card Funeral has left.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:27.530
All SARGs, evacuate the area.

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:29.700
Prepare for EMP.

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.700
All planes out of trajectory.

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:35.880
No change in target and point of impact.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:39.150
Margin of error corrected
to plus or minus .051.

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:40.330
Coordinates still apply.

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:43.260
Fire.

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:39.210
Gravitational change
confirmed at point of impact.

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:42.150
Large scale gravitational shifts
reported in both arms.

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:44.880
Did he bend it?

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:46.780
All that power?

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:53.490
Get the EX-1.

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:56.920
We'll cut both its arms off
and break that energy field.

00:11:58.160 --> 00:11:58.840
Not good!

00:11:59.170 --> 00:12:00.300
Prepare for impact!

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:11.160
No!

00:12:30.460 --> 00:12:31.860
It's all right.

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:34.040
It's all right, Hattie.

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:39.770
Commander, are you okay?

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:41.050
Thank you, Captain.

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:49.280
Everyone all right?

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:51.100
Yes, ma'am, we're okay.

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:09.450
Damn!

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:13.170
If we can take its head off...

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:21.760
Stay away from Hattie!

00:13:32.090 --> 00:13:39.050
<i>I can feel on my frozen cheek the slight...</i>

00:13:39.050 --> 00:13:42.990
<i>...singing voice.</i>

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:50.040
<i>Where springs become summers,
and green meadows lie.</i>

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:56.040
<i>Where babbling brooks babble, and dragonflies fly.</i>

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:04.680
The EX-1 will finish it! Back him up!

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:06.680
Impossible! He can't!

00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:08.290
Yes, he can.

00:14:08.290 --> 00:14:09.560
I know he can...

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:19.070
I'll help you.

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:22.070
Mr. Fairy...

00:14:24.110 --> 00:14:25.530
Auxiliary power up.

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:26.950
And the Fefnir?

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:28.350
Not enough power.

00:14:28.350 --> 00:14:31.780
We'd only get one shot at 60% efficiency.

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:33.420
I don't care. Prepare to fire.

00:14:33.420 --> 00:14:34.520
It's no use.

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:36.690
The target's outside guidance range.

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:39.210
It's already at the center of the base.

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:41.840
There's still a way.

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:46.470
Accelerate the charge in
the chamber, reverse pressure...

00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:49.340
...then guide it vertically.

00:14:49.340 --> 00:14:50.720
Blow out the barrel?

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:52.560
We only have one shot anyway.

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:57.270
But we have to get around
its gravitational shifts.

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:04.990
Now! It can't use its arms now!

00:15:04.990 --> 00:15:06.780
This is our last chance with the Fefnir!

00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:13.870
Fire!

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:26.930
We did it!

00:15:26.930 --> 00:15:28.390
N-Not quite.

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:36.030
It recovers so fast.

00:15:44.900 --> 00:15:45.820
Frank!

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:22.080
Mr. Fairy!

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:24.730
Did it...

00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:26.040
Did it get him?

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:35.500
It's over.

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:44.150
Ryu, what's wrong?

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:45.140
Move!

00:16:45.140 --> 00:16:48.150
It's over, Maki...

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:49.100
Ryu, what's wrong?

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:18.970
W-Why?

00:17:26.630 --> 00:17:28.690
Are you helping Mr. Fairy?

00:17:29.530 --> 00:17:32.200
You're not a bad one.

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:34.830
You're a good fairy!

00:17:34.830 --> 00:17:36.580
You actually are good!

00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:41.460
Why don't you ever die?

00:17:47.150 --> 00:17:48.710
Ryu...

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:50.410
Sue, Guenevere, back me up!

00:17:55.320 --> 00:17:57.500
I can't leave it up to just Ryu and Frank!

00:17:57.620 --> 00:17:58.620
Hold on!

00:17:58.620 --> 00:17:59.990
You're not hogging the credit!

00:17:59.990 --> 00:18:00.990
Right.

00:18:00.990 --> 00:18:04.930
If you're two ranks above me,
I'll never catch up!

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:06.310
All right.

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:19.550
Why?

00:18:19.550 --> 00:18:22.250
Why don't you die?

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:23.150
Ryu!

00:18:26.090 --> 00:18:26.790
Here I come!

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:27.870
That big hole!

00:18:29.660 --> 00:18:31.040
I'm switching off the limiter!

00:18:32.060 --> 00:18:33.210
Maximum engine output!

00:18:40.530 --> 00:18:42.260
Move!

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:49.040
The motors are interfering with the gravity.

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:50.930
The power field is fluctuating!

00:18:51.110 --> 00:18:52.210
Impossible.

00:18:52.210 --> 00:18:55.100
The SARGs will give out
before the gravity field!

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:56.830
Mr. Fairy...

00:19:21.040 --> 00:19:23.470
Ryu, what are you doing?

00:19:23.740 --> 00:19:25.930
Frank saved you, didn't he?

00:19:26.150 --> 00:19:27.850
Saved me?

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:28.890
Hurry it up!

00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:35.410
Follow us!

00:19:39.020 --> 00:19:42.610
The rate of power collapse
has moved up 34.54%.

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:45.040
You can do it, everyone...

00:20:30.190 --> 00:20:31.190
Spread out!

00:21:22.230 --> 00:21:23.960
Tell me.

00:21:23.960 --> 00:21:26.940
What in the world are you?

00:21:31.770 --> 00:21:33.970
We were able to defend...

00:21:33.970 --> 00:21:35.440
...our home.

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:39.240
But we left a big job for the landscapers.

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:41.830
Captain!

00:21:43.980 --> 00:21:44.950
You're hurt badly...

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:47.250
No, don't worry...

00:21:49.620 --> 00:21:52.880
You did a good job.

00:21:57.160 --> 00:21:58.630
Everyone's got funny faces.

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:11.680
Even you, Walton!

00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:15.180
Like all the fairies Grandpa made.

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:17.520
I see... I found it!

00:22:17.520 --> 00:22:21.250
This must be
the real land of the fairies...

00:22:22.290 --> 00:22:25.080
It's right here...

00:22:26.930 --> 00:22:31.920
Despair and Hope

00:22:32.670 --> 00:22:36.800
The times of confusion will never end,
just like an arctic night.

00:22:36.800 --> 00:22:39.140
And truths are stones on the road...

00:22:39.140 --> 00:22:42.230
Too numerous to count
and scattered about...

00:22:43.040 --> 00:22:45.900
Next time,
Hope and Chaos.
